<title>GERMANY: West German Dec adjusted unemployment rises 22,000.</title>
<headline>West German Dec adjusted unemployment rises 22,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Dec 96	  Nov 96	   Dec 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.961 mln     2.825 mln	2.678 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		2.948 mln     2.926 mln	2.669 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +22,000	 +35,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		9.6 pct	 9.2 pct	  8.7 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	157,882	 171,015	  166,528</p>
<p> Vacancies		   221,990	 219,176	  211,158</p>
<p> Change in number in work Oct  96	Sept 96</p>
<p>				 -37,000	  -42,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
